Package: kpclientd
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: katzenpost (<< 0.0.111~)
Replaces: katzenpost (<< 0.0.111~)
Description: client daemon of the Katzenpost mix network
 kpclientd connects to a Katzenpost mix network and lets client
 applications send and receive messages through it over a local socket.
 .
 It gets a system and a user unit, both shipped disabled and unstarted.
 kpclientd.toml and thinclient.toml hold no secrets and are conffiles;
 editing them points the client daemon at another network.

Package: katzenpost
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: kpclientd
Description: mix network servers and tools of Katzenpost
 The katzenpost binaries for running a mix network, each installed under
 a kp prefix so that no generic name is claimed in /usr/bin: kpserver,
 kpdirauth, kpcourier and kpreplica, and the kpconfig, kpgenconfig,
 kpgenkeypair, kpgeometry, kpsphinx, kpping, kpmotd, kpfetch,
 kpecho-plugin and kphttp-proxy tools. The client daemon is in the
 kpclientd package.
 .
 kpserver, kpauthority and kpreplica are template units, so one host can
 run several of each. Every unit ships disabled and unstarted.
 .
 An instance named foo reads /etc/katzenpost/<role>/foo.toml and keeps its
 state in /var/lib/katzenpost/<role>/foo, mode 0700, so two instances
 never share a directory.
